CHAPTER V"

SANCTION PROVISIONS

Article 12 (1) Any person who intentionally does not provide protection to women and children resulting in the occurrence of violence, allows violence to occur, and or does not report and does not provide protection to victims, shall be subject to sanctions in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

2. If officials appointed to implement protection do not carry out their obligations and responsibilities, they shall be subject to sanctions in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;
3. PPT managers who carry out service tasks that violate service principles may be subject to sanctions in accordance with PPT internal mechanisms.
